✗ The snapshot executor violates line 6: firing `0` started while the epoch clock read 100;
the clocks move to wall 6 and injected epoch 120 while it is in flight, and the executor's epoch
reading stays at 100, so the value it writes next would be stamped 100.

✓ The CORE firing requirement CORE-022 and the VER requirements hold together. Example: the
reference firing relation; one rest set for VER-014 and VER-002 with the reference violations;
the reference verified net and expansion of VER-001, the verified-net function that builds that
net, and the reference verifier over it (VER-003), the reference environment verifier (VER-006),
the reference timed step (VER-004) and the reference XOR analysis on that expansion (VER-021);
the bounded witness phase of VER-025 with its pipeline; the reference P-invariant finder,
semiflow encoder, zone library, bound phase, counter rules, firing-bound phase and siphon search;
the reference `QuiescentCount` constructor; the reference colour-slot bound of NU-053; and the
witnesses of the W10 pipeline blocks. The skeleton of `spec_consistent_ver`.

✓ A fork that emits a new token carrying the consumed value satisfies CORE-052 on values,
while its tokens are not the consumed one: on `f2` with the stamped token `(7, 100)` delivered,
place 1 receives `(7, 0)`.

Every line of ENV-014 is exercised by the reference, on the test derivation's runs: (1) AC6:
with `t`'s action in flight, the net's only token is in no place and the answer is `some true`;
(2) after the completion is committed, nothing is in flight or queued and the answer is
`some false`, with the output token in place `1` (the restore point of the test derivation);
(3) AC9: the loop is blocked in its wait, the answer is `some false`, and the loop stays blocked;
(4) AC7: an event accepted while the loop waits, nothing in flight, the answer is `some true`;
(5) AC4: after a drain the answer is `none`; (6) after a close the answer is `none` (the test
derivation's 'call after close() and verify rejection'); (7) after an immediate termination the
answer is `none`; (8) line 6: a run from the initial state in which the action flushes a batch in
the wait, the answer is `some true` while the batch is queued and `some false` once step 1b has
deposited it, with the published token in place `1`.

✓ The reference executor with the Java and TypeScript emission meets EVT-011: every deposit
appends its tokens at the tail and reports one `TokenAdded` event per token, naming its place;
the boot and the starts report none, and a start only takes tokens.

